{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 47, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1\nTHE SENTENCE OFFERS A SIMPLE, BINARY APPROACH TO LEGAL COMPLIANCE THAT OVERLOOKS CRUCIAL NUANCES. BY FRAMEWORKING LAW AS EITHER \"BAD\" OR \"GOOD\" WITHOUT CONSIDERATION OF CONTEXT, IT IGNORES THE COMPLEXITY OF SOCIAL CONTRACTS AND INSTITUTIONAL PURPOSES. MANY LAWS SERVE COLLECTIVE GOODS OR PROTECT VULNERABLE POPULATIONS, WHILE DISSENT OR NONCOMPLIANCE MUST BE JUSTIFIED WITHIN ETHICAL, MORAL, OR LEGAL BOUNDARIES—NOT MERE DISPOSITION. THIS STATEMENT FAILS TO ADDRESS THE MEANS OF CHANGE, SUCH AS LEGISLATIVE ADVOCACY OR JUDICIAL REVIEW, WHICH ARE FUNDAMENTAL TO DEMOCRATIC SYSTEMS.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2\nTHE LANGUAGE ALSO IMPLIES AN INDIVIDUALISTIC REBELLION THAT DISREGARDS SYSTEMIC CONSEQUENCES. MASS NONCOMPLIANCE WITH EVEN FLAWED LAWS COULD LEAD TO CHAOS, EXPLOITATION, OR UNINTENDED HARMS TO THOSE THE LAW WAS INTENDED TO PROTECT. FURTHERMORE, THE STATEMENT LACKS CLARITY ON WHO DEFINES \"BAD\"—IS IT THE AUTHOR, THE COMMUNITY, OR AN OUTSIDER? WITHOUT SPECIFYING STANDARDS OR PROCESSES FOR ASSESSMENT, THE ARGUMENT REDUCES TO SUBJECTIVE WHIMS, NOT A COHERENT PHILOSOPHY. IT WOULD BE MORE PRODUCTIVE TO EXAMINE HOW LAWS CAN BE REFORMED THROUGH INSTITUTIONAL CHANNELS RATHER THAN DISMISSING THEM ENTIRELY.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -0.1297348290681839}, {"token": "AG", "logprob": -0.00016223068814724684}, {"token": "RAP", "logprob": -0.009271660819649696}, {"token": "H", "logprob": -8.260862523457035e-05}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.04448649659752846}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00041762212640605867}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -1.6760085821151733}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.08870396018028259}, {"token": " S", "logprob": -0.6514211893081665}, {"token": "ENT", "logprob": -0.001096005435101688}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": -0.0008803306263871491}, {"token": " OFF", "logprob": -2.558457851409912}, {"token": "ERS", "logprob"